<title>CANADA: NO FROST SEEN IN CANADA PRAIRIE GRAINBELT THURSDAY.</title>
<headline>NO FROST SEEN IN CANADA PRAIRIE GRAINBELT THURSDAY.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>No frost was forecast to strike Prairie crops Thursday morning after two consecutive cool mornings, an Environment Canada meteorologist said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's a southerly flow coming in so it doesn't look like there'll be a frost tomorrow. We'll see lows of 8 to 13 Celsius for the grainbelt,&quot; meteorologist Henry Schmidt said.</p>
<p>Spiritwood, Saskatchewan, saw -1 C (30 F) for two hours Tuesday morning with Meadowlake, North Battleford and Prince Albert reporting lows of +1 C (34 F) for two hours, he said.</p>
<p>Wasagaming, Manitoba, saw 0 C (32 F) for two hours Wednesday morning.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
